    "explanation": "Both of you are substantially right about the driving, but the record cannot carry a money ruling as it stands, so the SGD 9.00 in dispute is held rather than collected or refunded. On the driving, the rider is correct: EV-GPS-02858 is a complete, unimpaired trace (218 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), so none of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires and no independent corroboration is required. It measures 27.69 km against the booked optimal of 21.3 km on EV-TRIP-02858 - an excess of 6.39 km, 30.0% of optimal - which establishes a deviation under POL-RD-01 (both limbs pass: >20% and >0.8 km) but is not material (neither >50% nor >8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 profile check is not engaged. On that measurement the POL-RD-02 arithmetic over EV-FARE-02858 (METERED; surge multiplier 1.000 read from that artifact alone) gives a recomputed fare of 28.639 against a charged total of 35.52, i.e. 6.881, rounded up to SGD 6.90 - not the full SGD 9.00 the rider contests, and the rider's advocate rightly concedes the SGD 6.90 figure. The driver's explanation 'Followed navigation' is unsupported: no traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-02858-01 is MISSING, carries no payload and has weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run; because the driver cites no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) makes that a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) escalation on its own, and his excuse simply carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The obstacle is not the driving but identification. The fare breakdown EV-FARE-02858 carries two trip identifiers that disagree: TRP-02858 on the artifact itself, and TRP-02758 inside its own payload, which does not match the TRP-02858 on EV-TRIP-02858 and EV-GPS-02858. POL-RD-10(2) directs that no final ruling be issued where the trip identifiers on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown do not all match, and under POL-GEN-03 an escalation is terminal: it replaces the ruling, no refund or compensation issues, and the disputed amount is held. What would resolve it is a corrected fare breakdown whose trip identifier matches TRP-02858, or a payments-ledger confirmation of which trip the SGD 35.52 charge belongs to. Nothing else in the money block moves: there are no ERP gantry lines (off-optimal-route ERP 0.00), no airport surcharge, and no charge line without a counterpart, so POL-RD-09(4) has no billing-integrity finding to refer and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises from a non-material deviation. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04."
